From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:50:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 208/274] CED row copy: every 1- to 8-byte element type, and
 the key owners declare

The copy reads elements by size, so it takes every 1-, 2-, 4- and 8-byte type
the packing ABI can be given (uint8 sources are among its tests).
copy_rows_key is the kernel's arguments for a source layout, used by the copy
itself; packed_copy_rows_key is the same for packed rows of a shape, which an
owner declares for preparation, so the two cannot drift apart.

